// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row closure_fnonce_cond_call_untaken_leak (tier 1). AN
// `FnOnce` CLOSURE CALLED IN ONE BRANCH LOSES ITS CAPTURE ON THE OTHER.
//
// `let f = move || -> i64 { let t: D = x; return t.v; }; if c { r = f(); }`
// destroys `x` exactly once when the branch is taken and NOT AT ALL when it is
// not. Rust destroys it once either way: the closure owns the capture, the call
// consumes the closure, and a conditionally-consumed local carries a drop flag.
//
// ROOT, by symbol: the handover this round installed is set-based and has NO
// BRANCH MERGE. `SemaChecker::mark_moved_deferred_only` (src/compiler/
// sema_impl.hpp) releases the source's obligation by erasing the capture from
// `closure_owned_drop_` — a plain `std::set<std::string>` that
// `elaborate_cond_moves` never saves, reverts or merges — so the release made
// while lowering the TAKEN arm stands on the untaken arm too, and the drop the
// source was still holding is emitted nowhere.
//
// THE ARM THAT ALREADY EXISTS: #118's conditional-move elaboration
// (`SemaChecker::elaborate_cond_moves` / `Frame::cond_move_flags` /
// `guard_with_flag`, src/compiler/sema.cpp) gives a local moved on SOME
// reaching path a runtime flag and emits its destructor GUARDED. It is proven
// live on the plain spelling: `let x: D = …; if c { eat(x); } else { … }`
// reads 1 on BOTH arms today (hand programs cx7/cx8, this build). It is not
// reached here because `emit_frame_drops`' flag arm is written
// `cf != frame.cond_move_flags.end() && !closure_owned_drop_.count(n)` — the
// closure arm is DELIBERATELY given precedence, with a measured reason in its
// own comment (a `move` closure inside ANY branch, `if true` included, cleared
// its flag on the taken path and LOST the capture). So the fix is not to drop
// that precedence but to make the DEFERRED subset flag-bearing: the release is
// a conditional move of the capture, and it is the only member of
// `closure_owned_drop_` for which that is true.
//
// ⚠ NOT A REGRESSION. Measured identically (count 0) on the base binary
// febd1aa6e49ae30c 43, where the leak came from the OLD delegation instead —
// sema's `if (body_moved_outer.count(...)) continue;` stood the source down on
// both arms. The unconditional spellings moved 0 -> 1 this round; this one did
// not move at all.
//
// ⚠ THE ORACLE IS A DESTRUCTOR COUNT: today 0, exit 1; correct is 1, exit 0.
// The taken twin is pass/closure_fnonce_capture_drop_never_called's sibling
// shape and reads 1 on this build.
package closure_fnonce_cond_call_untaken_leak;

struct D { v: i64, c: *mut i64 }
impl Drop for D { fn drop(self: &mut D) { unsafe { *self.c = *self.c + self.v; } } }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
    let p: *mut i64 = &mut n;
    let mut r: i64 = -1i64;
    {
        let x: D = D { v: 1i64, c: p };
        let f = move || -> i64 { let t: D = x; return t.v; };
        if n == 7i64 { r = f(); } else { r = 5i64; }
    }
    let got: i64 = unsafe { n };
    if got != 1i64 { return 1i32; }
    if r != 5i64 { return 3i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
